---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Car Rental App Redesign";
const description =
  "A customer-focused mobile booking experience designed to make finding and reserving the right car feel faster and clearer.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm tracking-wide text-text-light">
      <a href="/projects" class="hover:text-primary">← Projects</a>
    </p>
    <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] text-text-light uppercase">UX/UI Design</p>
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-black text-text-dark md:text-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-text-light">{description}</p>

    <img
      src="/images/projects/car-rental-app-redesign/cover.webp"
      alt="Car rental mobile app screens showing search, vehicle selection, extras, and payment"
      width="1200"
      height="468"
      class="mb-10 w-full rounded-lg bg-light object-contain p-4"
      loading="eager"
    />

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-text-light">
      This five-month solo project explored how a car rental app could make the booking process more approachable.
      The work focused on helping customers compare vehicles, understand costs, and reserve a car in fewer,
      more predictable steps.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10 text-text-light">
      The redesign balances speed with the information people need to make a confident decision, from useful filters
      and clearer price breakdowns to a less disruptive guest checkout experience.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Approach</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-text-light">
      Competitive analysis and journey mapping surfaced friction around search, pricing, promotions, and payment.
      Low-fidelity sketches then tested alternative list and detail layouts before the strongest direction moved into
      a polished interface.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10 text-text-light">
      An interactive prototype covered the full journey: filtering and comparing cars, selecting extras, reviewing
      the price breakdown, and completing payment.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Focus areas</h2>
    <ul class="mb-10 list-disc pl-5 text-text-light space-y-1">
      <li>User journey and opportunity mapping</li>
      <li>Information architecture and booking flow</li>
      <li>Wireframes, visual design, and prototyping</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
